messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2025,
      "event": "Frontier AI systems achieve autonomous multi-step reasoning and scientific research capabilities",
      "detail": "Large language models and robotic agents begin planning and executing complex projects without human oversight, accelerating discovery while raising acute concerns about job displacement and loss of control."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions peak and begin a sustained decline",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, nuclear, and carbon capture technologies reach cost parity with fossil fuels in most markets, though accumulated warming continues to drive extreme weather."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "First therapies that partially reverse biological aging enter clinical use",
      "detail": "Senolytic drugs and gene therapies that clear senescent cells extend healthy human lifespan by decades, fundamentally altering demographics, healthcare systems, and retirement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Autonomous vehicles and general-purpose robots eliminate most driving and manual labor jobs",
      "detail": "AI-driven automation displaces hundreds of millions of workers, forcing governments to experiment with universal basic income and post-work economic models."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "First permanent human base on Mars is established",
      "detail": "A self-sustaining settlement of 100 scientists and engineers begins operations on Mars, marking humanity's transition to a multi-planetary species."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Arctic Ocean becomes ice-free in summer and the Gulf Stream weakens significantly",
      "detail": "Climate tipping points trigger cascading effects including disrupted weather patterns, agricultural failures in the Northern Hemisphere, and accelerated sea level rise."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) is achieved by at least one laboratory",
      "detail": "AI systems surpass human capability in all cognitive domains, triggering a global race to align the technology with human values or exploit it for economic and military dominance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Commercial fusion power plants connect to major electrical grids",
      "detail": "Abundant clean energy enables large-scale desalination, carbon capture, and energy-intensive industries, though geopolitical tensions over energy access persist."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces allow direct neural control of computers and communication",
      "detail": "Non-invasive BCIs enable paralyzed patients to type and speak at normal speeds, paving the way for cognitive enhancement and direct brain-to-brain communication."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Sea level rise reaches half a meter, displacing hundreds of millions from coastal zones",
      "detail": "Low-lying island nations become uninhabitable and major cities like Miami, Shanghai, and Dhaka face chronic flooding, triggering mass climate migration and resource conflicts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Average life expectancy in wealthy nations exceeds 100 years",
      "detail": "Regenerative medicine and organ replacement push lifespans far beyond historical norms, creating multi-generational households and straining pension and inheritance systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "World population peaks at approximately 10.4 billion then begins to decline",
      "detail": "Urbanization, education, and voluntary low fertility in Asia and Africa drive a slow demographic contraction, easing pressure on planetary resources."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Germline gene editing eliminates most hereditary diseases",
      "detail": "CRISPR and successor technologies eradicate conditions like Huntington's disease and cystic fibrosis from the human gene pool, sparking ethical debates over genetic enhancement and social inequality."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Post-scarcity economies emerge in advanced nations due to full automation",
      "detail": "AI and robotics produce all goods and services at near-zero marginal cost, making money largely obsolete in some regions while creating new social hierarchies based on status and access."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "First large rotating space habitat (O'Neill cylinder) is completed in Earth orbit",
      "detail": "The habitat provides artificial gravity, agriculture, and industry for 10,000 residents, demonstrating that humanity can live sustainably off-world."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Asteroid mining begins delivering platinum group metals and water to orbit",
      "detail": "Space resources crash terrestrial commodity prices, destabilizing mining economies while enabling massive construction projects like solar power satellites and larger habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Genetically adapted humans form a distinct Martian population",
      "detail": "Humans engineered for low gravity and high radiation become reproductively isolated from Earth humans, creating a new branch of the human family tree."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "A catastrophic existential event reduces the human population by 30 to 50 percent",
      "detail": "An engineered pandemic, limited nuclear exchange, asteroid impact, or unaligned AI incident kills billions and severs global supply chains, triggering civilizational stress."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Global civilization fragments into regional powers during a dark age",
      "detail": "Technological regression lasts two centuries in some regions, with knowledge preserved only in isolated universities, digital archives, and religious institutions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "A supervolcanic eruption causes a global volcanic winter and population bottleneck",
      "detail": "An eruption like Yellowstone or Campi Flegrei injects sulfur aerosols into the stratosphere, collapsing agriculture worldwide and reducing the human population to perhaps ten million."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "A technological renaissance begins as societies recover",
      "detail": "Surviving populations rediscover preserved knowledge and develop new biotechnologies that leapfrog previous industrial paradigms, rebuilding civilization on new foundations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "Self-replicating von Neumann probes begin systematic asteroid belt industrialization",
      "detail": "Autonomous robots mine asteroids and use the raw materials to build more robots and habitats, growing the space economy exponentially without human labor."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Molecular nanotechnology enables atomically precise manufacturing",
      "detail": "Diamondoid materials and nanoscale medical robots become available, allowing construction of ultra-strong structures and cures for virtually all diseases at the cellular level."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "First interstellar probe arrives at the Proxima Centauri system",
      "detail": "A probe traveling at 0.1c completes its 42-year journey to the nearest star, transmitting data about Proxima Centauri b and demonstrating interstellar travel is feasible."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Mind uploading becomes feasible, creating the first digital human consciousness",
      "detail": "Human minds are copied to digital substrates, creating immortal post-human entities that can travel as data at light speed and exist in simulated environments."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "Post-human digital intelligences vastly outnumber biological humans",
      "detail": "Uploaded minds running on stellar-scale computers drive most scientific and economic activity, while biological humans become a minority, often living in protected reserves or virtual worlds."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "A matrioshka brain is constructed around a nearby star",
      "detail": "A computer the size of a solar system harnesses a star's total energy output to simulate more minds than have ever lived on Earth simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Earth becomes uninhabitable due to solar brightening, forcing final evacuation",
      "detail": "The Sun's increasing luminosity raises global temperatures beyond the tolerance of complex life, so remaining biological humans migrate to terraformed moons of Jupiter and Saturn or artificial habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Solar system population reaches one trillion in space habitats",
      "detail": "Millions of O'Neill cylinders, rotating asteroids, and domed cities across the inner and outer solar system house a trillion post-human inhabitants."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "A Dyson swarm captures 10 percent of the Sun's total energy output",
      "detail": "Trillions of solar collectors orbit the Sun, beaming power to habitats and computation nodes across the system, marking the solar system as a Kardashev Type I civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Generation ships and seed probes are launched toward nearby star systems",
      "detail": "Vessels carrying frozen embryos, uploaded minds, or self-replicating factories depart for twenty stars within fifty light years, beginning the interstellar diaspora."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Diverse post-human civilizations thrive throughout the solar system and nearby stars",
      "detail": "Homo sapiens as a biological species is extinct, replaced by descendant intelligences—digital, synthetic, or genetically engineered—that continue to expand and evolve across the galaxy."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity's near future is dominated by climate change, artificial intelligence, and biotechnology, with a substantial risk of a population-crashing catastrophe between 2400 and 2600 that could cause extinction or a multi-century dark age. If we survive these bottlenecks, we likely transition into post-human digital or space-dwelling intelligences that persist and expand across the solar system, though biological Homo sapiens will almost certainly be extinct well before year 10000."
}
